# Azure Virtual Machine: xfusion-vm

**Objective:** Deploy an Ubuntu 22.04 LTS VM in Azure with a 30GB Standard HDD and SSH access.

**Requirements:**

1. Use the existing resource group.
2. VM name: `xfusion-vm`
3. Region: West US
4. OS image: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
5. VM size: Standard_B1s
6. Attach a default NSG allowing inbound SSH (port 22)
7. OS disk: 30 GB, Standard HDD
8. Rest of the settings remain default

**Azure CLI Commands:**

```bash
# Log in to Azure
az login

# Create the VM
az vm create \
  --resource-group <RESOURCE_GROUP> \
  --name xfusion-vm \
  --image UbuntuLTS \
  --size Standard_B1s \
  --admin-username azureuser \
  --ssh-key-values ~/.ssh/datacenter-kp.pub \
  --nsg-rule SSH \
  --os-disk-size-gb 30 \
  --storage-sku Standard_LRS \
  --location westus

# SSH into the VM
ssh -i ~/.ssh/datacenter-kp azureuser@<PUBLIC_IP>

